# God Rest Ye Merry Gentlemen, arranged by Claude and SZ. An off-beat bass alone, then a broken beat under the minor-key carol.
title: God Rest Ye Merry Gentlemen
composer: Traditional (English)
arranger: Claude & SZ
about: One of the oldest English carols. "God rest ye merry" meant "God keep you happy", so the comma belongs after merry. In A Christmas Carol, a boy starts singing it at Scrooge's keyhole and Scrooge chases him away.
year: traditional
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: E minor
style: techno
tempo: 126
time: 4/4

